            <ArticleTitle>Brodie's abscess--an uncommon cause of leg pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>183-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">03.2008/JCPSP.183184</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A rare case of Brodie's abscess of distal left tibia is presented in a child which was initially missed on clinical grounds alone. Differentiation from different bone neoplasms was done on radiological grounds. The patient was managed surgically with high dose intravenous antibiotics. Brodie's abscess is very rarely encountered in our reporting of X-rays.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
